## One thing I did not fix

The same single-component error is live in two other artifacts, which hold parameters and formulas rather than worked examples, so they fell outside this pass's stated scope. Recorded in `CCG_CONTENT_REVIEW.md` with exact cells:

- **Payslip generator, `J40` on both Belgium (EN) and Belgium (NL)**: `=IF(J35<=3403.62,-127.54,0)`. Wrong three ways — component A only, grants the **full maximum anywhere below the upper limit** (precisely the error Module 5.1.1's "Correction of record" warns against), and 3403.62 is the September row. An employee on 3,000.00 gets a 127.54 bonus that should be a degressive partial amount. This one is executable, not descriptive, so it's the more urgent of the two.
- **WTC**, `Version Control!C25`, `Wage Type Catalogue!F55`, `Wage Type Catalogue!F303`, `Tax Credit!B6` — all present 127.54 / 137.74 as the whole bonus, with component B absent.
